  "id": "psychodynamic-approach",
  "term": "psychodynamic approach",
  "definition": "In this context, a psychodynamic approach is a way of understanding physical symptoms by exploring how emotional processes, such as unresolved grief, trauma, and unmet needs, may contribute to or worsen them. It emphasizes a collaborative investigation of the links between emotional life and bodily distress.",
